.TH BIOKIDS\-DAEMON 8 2026\-09\-30 "biokids 0.1.0" "BioKids"
.SH NAME
biokids\-daemon \- BioKids time keeping and enforcement
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B biokids\-daemon
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR level ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B biokids\-daemon
counts each child's screen time and enforces the limits a parent set:
it warns before time runs out, ends the session when it does, and keeps the
record the parent panel shows.
It runs as root under
.BR systemd (1)
as
.B biokids\-daemon.service
and is not meant to be started by hand.
.PP
If it fails,
.B biokids\-lockdown.service
locks every child session; see
.BR biokids\-admin (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the configuration from
.I file
instead of
.IR /etc/biokids/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
One of DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-logind
Run without systemd\-logind.
For development only.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run a single tick and exit.
For smoke tests only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/biokids/config.toml
Machine configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/biokids/biokids.db
Settings, time history and the audit log.
.TP
.I /run/biokids/daemon.sock
The socket the panel and
.BR biokids\-admin (8)
talk to.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR biokids\-admin (8),
.BR biokids\-panel (8)
